<title>AUSTRALIA: Westpac shares surge as buyback extended.</title>
<headline>Westpac shares surge as buyback extended.</headline>
<dateline>SYDNEY 1997-05-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in Westpac Banking Corporation soared on Friday after the bank said it planned to buy back 50 million shares or 2.8 percent of its issued capital.</p>
<p>By 2.25 p.m. (0425 GMT), Westpac shares were up 22 cents at A$7.13, their highest level in a month. The shares were trading five cents higher prior to the scheme's announcement.</p>
<p>Westpac said the new scheme in effect extended a buyback scheme announced in November 1996 but which had to be suspended during negotiations with the Bank of Melbourne which Westpac is bidding A$9.75 a share for.</p>
<p>--Sdyeny Newsroom 61-02 9373 1810</p>
